WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.920
A dusty warehouse.

2
00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:04.490
A stack of unsold hardbacks.

3
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.200
1925.

4
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:13.980
The first printing is 20,870 copies, and
it takes until June 1926 to sell out.

5
00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:20.710
The calendar flips to 1940, then 1945:
crates of small paperbacks loaded onto

6
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.000
army trucks.

7
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.970
155,000 copies, for the troops.

8
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.800
Later, a classroom.

9
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:30.310
Every student holds the same book.

10
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.700
It sold poorly in 1925.

11
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.480
Now it's a classic.

12
00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:35.910
So what changed?

13
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:39.320
In this mission, you'll step into
the Jazz Age it was written in:

14
00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:42.070
jazz, cars, and bootleg drink.

15
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.590
And you'll trace how critics have
read it differently over the decades,

16
00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.330
including on race.

17
00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:50.040
Your mission: work out what changed.
